mental regulations. Read more Administrative Secretary Ypsilanti College of Education Academic & Student Affairs Staff Full Time Opening on: Sep 2 2026 Closing on: Sep 16 2026 Provide secretarial services and administrative assistance to Dean, Executive Director, or equivalent-level administrator. Read more Athletic Academic Program Specialist Ypsilanti Intercollegiate Athletics Intercollegiate Athletics Staff Full Time Opening on: Sep 2 2026 Closing on: Sep 16 2026 Assist in the administration as well as the continuous development and implementation of a comprehensive support program for all student-athletes in compliance with University, MAC and NCAA regulations. Read more Assistant Professor (Special Education) Ypsilanti College of Education Academic & Student Affairs College of Education Faculty Full Time Opening on: Sep 1 2026 Closing on: Jan 10 2027 The Department of Special Education & Communication Sciences and Disorders, College of Education at Eastern Michigan University seeks applicants for a tenure track faculty position within its Special Education Program. The appointment will be at the rank of Assistant Professor with a start in Fall 2027.\n\nThe successful candidate will serve an eight-month, tenure-track appointment with summer employment contingent on student demand, funding, and contractual policies and procedures. A competitive salary will be based on qualifications and prior experience. Read more Part- Time Lecturer (College of Arts and Sciences) Ypsilanti College of Arts and Sciences Academic & Student Affairs College of Arts & Sciences Part Time Lecturer Opening on: Aug 31 2026 Closing on: Sep 17 2026 The Department of Mathematics & Statistics is seeking a part-time lecturer to teach specific Math & Stat courses. Read more Staff Graduate Assistant - MSHROD China Ypsilanti College of Business Academic & Student Affairs Graduate Assistant Temporary Opening on: Aug 31 2026 The scope of work potentially includes but is not limited to assisting with translations and communications with EMU partners in China, working with faculty in the EMU Management Department on their pedagogical and research activities pertaining to the MSHROD China program, and other office support type activities.\nThe Graduate Assistant receives a stipend and a tuition waiver. Read more STAFF GRADUATE ASSISTANT (SGA) Ypsilanti EMU Foundation and Advancement Advancement Graduate Assistant Opening on: Aug 25 2026 With the guidance of one or more staff members within The Career Development Center, perform a mixture of services in support of communication, technology, business operations or student affairs activities as more than 50% of their service. The Staff Graduate Assistant receives a stipend and tuition waiver subject to federal tax. Read more Part Time Lecturer Ypsilanti College of Arts and Sciences Academic & Student Affairs College of Arts & Sciences Part Time Lecturer Opening on: Aug 18 2026 Closing on: Sep 10 2026 The Eastern Michigan University School of Music & Dance invites applications for a Part-Time Lecturer in Dance for Fall 2026. Read more Academic Advisor (Pool) Ypsilanti Academic Programming and Services Academic & Student Affairs Staff Full Time Opening on: Aug 26 2026 Eastern Michigan University seeks to build a pool of qualified applicants for Academic Advising.  In this role, one will advise and counsel all assigned students on curriculum requirements, vocational information, scholarship and /or academic achievement problems. Read more Senior Analyst Budget Management Ypsilanti Business and Finance Business & Finance Staff Full Time Opening on: Aug 26 2026 Under limited supervision assist the Executive Director in the development of the University's general and auxiliary fund budgets including management, staff position control, benefit rate development, benefits budgets, revenues, analysis, evaluation, reporting, forecasting, and modeling. Read more College Data Analyst, Accreditation & Learning Assessment - CHHS Ypsilanti College of Health and Human Serv Academic & Student Affairs Staff Full Time Opening on: Aug 26 2026 Closing on: Sep 9 2026 Coordinate and implement the development and maintenance of databases, including analyzing and reporting data needed to support accreditation procedures and processes as well as student learning assessment, planning, and improvement activities within the assigned college. Read more Part Time Lecturer (Nursing) Ypsilanti College of Health and Human Serv Academic & Student Affairs College of Health & Human Services Adjunct Lecturer Opening on: Aug 21 2026 Closing on: Sep 13 2026 The School of Nursing is searching for part-time lecturers (PTLs) to work with our full-time faculty on an as-needed basis to teach clinical nursing courses. Read more Officer Campus Police Ypsilanti Public Safety Public Safety Staff Full Time Opening on: Aug 20 2026 Closing on: Oct 20 2026 Perform activities which ensure the safety of and provide protection and related services to the campus community including programs in law enforcement, community policing, health and safety, parking and traffic, crime prevention and suppression and in-service training. Read more Officer Campus Police Ypsilanti Public Safety Public Safety Staff Full Time Opening on: Aug 20 2026 Closing on: Oct 20 2026 Perform activities which ensure the safety of and provide protection and related services to the campus community including programs in law enforcement, community policing, health and safety, parking and traffic, crime prevention and suppression and in-service training. Read more Graduate Assistant - School of Nursing Ypsilanti College of Health and Human Serv Academic & Student Affairs Graduate Assistant Opening on: Jul 28 2026 The School of Nursing is seeking a motivated and detail-oriented Graduate Assistant (GA) to support teaching, research, and program operations. The GA will work closely with the Nursing Skills Lab Supervisor, faculty, staff, and students to enhance the learning environment and contribute to the mission of the School of Nursing. This is an on-campus position located at Eastern Michigan University in Ypsilanti, Michigan. Read more Assistant Coach - Women's Rowing Ypsilanti Intercollegiate Athletics Intercollegiate Athletics Staff Full Time Opening on: Aug 13 2026 Closing on: Sep 13 2026 Assist the Head Coach in the recruitment, counseling, conditioning, training and coaching of the rowing team. Read more Full-Time Lecturer (Social Work) Ypsilanti College of Health and Human Serv Academic & Student Affairs College of Health & Human Services Full Time Lecturer Opening on: Aug 7 2026 Closing on: Sep 11 2026 Teach specific courses within the School of Social Work. Background in Social Work and familiarity with the curriculum and teaching is essential. Preferred LLMSW or LMSW. Read more Graduate Assistant (Fashion Marketing) Ypsilanti Research Admin and Grad School Academic & Student Affairs Graduate Assistant Opening on: Jul 30 2026 Position Summary\nThe School of Technology & Professional Services Management invites applications for a\nGraduate Assistant (GA) to support the Fashion Marketing Innovation Program. This position\nprovides instructional, laboratory, and program support while offering valuable professional\nexperience in higher education and the fashion industry. The successful candidate will work\nclosely with faculty and students in apparel construction, textiles, product development, and\nfashion merchandising. The position is 50% for Fall 2026. Read more University Registrar Ypsilanti Enrollment Management Enrollment Management Staff Full Time Opening on: Jun 18 2026 Reporting to the Vice President for Enrollment Management, the Registrar serves as a strategic leader in advancing the institution’s enrollment management vision and student success priorities. As the institutional steward of academic records, the Registrar builds and leads a modern, student-centered operation that supports recruitment, retention, persistence, and degree completion through data-informed decision-making, process innovation, and cross-functional collaboration. The role is responsible for ensuring compliant, efficient, and technology-enabled registrar services while fostering a culture of accountability, continuous improvement, service excellence, and organizational change management across the student lifecycle. Read more Police Dispatcher Ypsilanti Public Safety Public Safety Staff Full Time Opening on: Jul 17 2026 Closing on: Sep 17 2026 Receive and dispatch emergency and non-emergency calls and alarms for police officers and other emergency personnel. Maintain a safety link between the department, officers, and the University community. EMU Dispatch is a single position primary public safety answering point (receives all 911 calls) for the University community. Read more Graduate Teacher Assistant (Children’s Institute) Ypsilanti Student Life Academic & Student Affairs Graduate Assistant Opening on: Jun 5 2026 Graduate Assistant, Children’s Institute, Teacher Assistant\n\nAssist in developing, planning, implementing and evaluating developmentally appropriate classroom activities for a specific age group of young children. Assist in supervising, training and evaluating student staff. Read more Athletics Camp Employee Ypsilanti Intercollegiate Athletics Intercollegiate Athletics Temporary Opening on: May 21 2026 Assist with the operations for the assigned athletics camp. Read more Building Automation Specialist Ypsilanti Facilities Business & Finance Staff Full Time Opening on: Oct 7 2025 Position is responsible for the monitoring, adjustment, programming, repair, and maintenance of heating, ventilation, air conditioning, and refrigeration (HVAC/R) automation and building integration systems. Position requires a variety of skilled and technical work related to the maintenance, repair, programming, and installation of HVAC/R automation and building integration systems and associated components. Read more Carpenter Ypsilanti Facilities Business & Finance Staff Full Time Opening on: Sep 11 2025 Perform skilled carpentry work in the fabrication, installation, and repair of structures and fixtures of wood, plywood, plastics, and other composition materials. Read more Teacher II Ypsilanti Student Life Academic & Student Affairs Staff Full Time Opening on: Sep 10 2025 Develop, plan, implement, and evaluate developmentally appropriate classroom activities for a specific age group of children. Supervise practicum students and work with faculty from Teacher Education in the Academic component of the institute. Read more Roofer Ypsilanti Facilities Business & Finance Custodial, Operations, & Facilities Staff Full Time Opening on: Nov 5 2024 Perform skilled roofing work. Read more Elevator Repair/Control Specialist Ypsilanti Facilities Business & Finance Staff Full Time Opening on: Nov 4 2024 Eastern Michigan University Is looking to recruit a dynamic workforce in order to operate, service and maintain elevator systems throughout the University campus. Read more Displaying 1 - 30 of 32 in total ‹ 1 2 › Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Report a Title IX Incident Accessibility Privacy Statement Annual Security Report Copyright © 2022 All Rights Reserved by Eastern Michigan University . Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept"
