      "description": "Institutional Research Analyst, Senior (IRIM) - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Home Working at EMU Benefits & Wellness About HR Existing Applicant Log-in Kiosk mode Institutional Research Analyst, Senior (IRIM) Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Inst Research and Accreditation Academic & Student Affairs Staff Full Time Opening on: Sep 8 2026 Closing on: Sep 22 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Institutional Research Analyst, Senior (IRIM) Employee Classification: PE Pay Grade: PT 10 Division: Academic and Student Affairs Subdivision: Institutional Res and Info Mgt Department: Inst Research and Accreditation Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary Develop and maintain systems that enhance the utility of the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) data warehouse. Develop and maintain online and automated reporting facilities. Provide statistical support and enrollment forecasting. Collect and audit primary and secondary data sources to assure accuracy of data for analysis. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Develop and manage web-based interfaces and procedures that provide access data in the data warehouse. Provide expert design and Web development for IRIM. Project management, design and testing of systems within a data warehouse environment. Provide database administration management & support. Manage and design online templates for academic program review. Compile and manage complex data sets and other information in support of institutional studies. Identify, gather, analyze, and organize institutional data to provide accurate and timely information. Prepare student/faculty/enrollment annual reports. Analyze and report data from the data warehouse when responding to ad hoc information requests. Respond to information requests from governmental, private and public institutions and internal sources. Work with the IRIM team to develop online reports for the data warehouse. Provide assistance to IRIM in identifying appropriate data collection to ensure reliable, appropriate, and legal use of institutional information. Perform related departmental duties as required, and upon the request of the Assistant Vice President and Executive Director of Institutional Research and Information Management. Minimum Qualifications: Knowledge of quantitative and analytical process, including information systems, typically acquired through the completion of a Master's Degree in computer science, management information systems or related field or a combination of formal education and experience is necessary. Proven proficiency in statistical analyses and in the use of SPSS or SAS software is required. Advanced skills in the design and implementation of quantitative and qualitative research typically acquired through at least five years progressively more responsible and complex experience is required. Familiarity with UNIX operating system, Oracle database and industry-standard web application development tools, such as PHP, is required. Experience using Microsoft Access, relational databases and/or visual basic programming is required. Demonstrated experience with data base management systems and concepts is preferred. Ability to handle multiple tasks efficiently and with attention to detail, and meet deadlines is essential. Strong written and oral communication skills are mandatory. Preferred Qualifications: N/A Special Instructions: N/A Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert 303c64fd Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Inst Research and Accreditation Inst Research and Accreditation Categories Academic & Student Affairs Academic & Student Affairs First Name (required) c49a4389 Last Name (required) 924f4f54 Email (required) eeee88