    "https://careers.emich.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-special-education-ypsilanti-michigan-united-states-6bd072ec-b09e-4c53-9e4d-9ece88350c46": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Special Education)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Special Education) - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Home Working at EMU Benefits & Wellness About HR Existing Applicant Log-in Kiosk mode Assistant Professor (Special Education) Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States College of Education Academic & Student Affairs College of Education Faculty Full Time Opening on: Sep 1 2026 Closing on: Jan 10 2027 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Assistant Professor (Special Education) Employee Classification: FA - Faculty 16 and 24 Pay Pay Grade: FA 01 Division: Academic and Student Affairs Subdivision: Spec Ed and Comm Sci and Disorders Department: College of Education Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary The Department of Special Education & Communication Sciences and Disorders, College of Education at Eastern Michigan University, seeks applicants for a tenure-track faculty position within its Special Education Program. The appointment will be at the rank of Assistant Professor with a start in Fall 2027. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Principal Duties and Responsibilities : • Design and deliver in-person, hybrid, remote (e.g., satellite locations), and online instruction within two or more of the program’s current categorical disability areas (undergraduate and graduate levels) for which its special education administration specialist degree may be one of them, as well as within the program’s new forthcoming comprehensive undergraduate licensure pathway. • Design curriculum and enact pedagogy that reflect and support current trends of best practices, inclusive excellence, diversity, equity, state standards, and the special education programmatic needs of local K-12 school districts. • Provide academic and scholarly research advising to undergraduate and graduate students. • Engage in research and scholarly activities relative to the university’s R2 ranking and in accordance with the program’s criteria for tenure and promotion. • Provide service at the program, department, college, and university levels. • Meet all contractual obligations for tenure-track faculty. Minimum Qualifications: Required Qualifications: • Doctoral degree in Special Education or related field from an accredited institution, completed and conferred by date of appointment and no later than one week prior to the start of the 2027-2028 academic year. • Three or more years of P-12 special education teaching experiences related to the appointment. • Experience in and/or knowledge about the preparation of special education teacher candidates from traditional and non-traditional backgrounds, including first-generation, urban, and second-career/adult learners, as well as in-service educators pursuing advanced credentials • Experience in and/or knowledge about in-person, hybrid, remote, and/or online (asynchronous and/or synchronous) instructional design and delivery. • Experience in and/or knowledge about how to address diversity, equity, and inclusion within a special education teacher preparation program, including within a special education administration specialist degree (if applicable). • An emergent/active scholarly agenda related to the appointment and the program’s criteria for tenure and promotion. Preferred Qualifications: Desired Qualifications: • Previous higher education teaching experience related to the appointment • Experience with acquiring or pursuing external research funding Special Instructions: All applications must be made online at https://caereers.emich.edu/jobs. Applicants must submit the following materials for consideration: 1. A cover letter that addresses each of the above listed required and preferred qualifications. Particular attention should detail a teaching philosophy and approach to the design and delivery of instruction related to this position. Applicants without a conferred doctoral degree from an accredited institution at time of applying must also detail a list of doctoral/dissertation benchmarks and dates leading up to an anticipated date of graduation. 2. A detailed curriculum vitae; and 3. The names, titles, professional mailing addresses, email addresses, and telephone numbers of at least three references, but no more than five references Applicants without a conferred doctoral degree from an accredited institution at time of applying must include and identify their dissertation chair as one of the references. For more information contact Dr. John Palladino, search committee chair, 734.487.2769 or jpalladi@emich.edu or Dr. Jackie McGinnis, Department Head, 734-4873300 or jmcginnis@emich.edu Appointment Percentage: 100%% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert 63ee73fc Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Education College of Education Categories Academic & Student Affairs College of Education Academic & Student Affairs College of Education First Name (required) d70e6f60 Last Name (required) 22f99285 Email (required) 53946fa6 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Institutional Research Analyst, Senior (IRIM) Inst Research and Accreditation Develop and maintain systems that enhance the utility of the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) data warehouse. Develop and maintain online and automated reporting facilities and interactive dashboards. Provide statistical support and enrollment forecasting. Collect and audit primary and secondary data sources to assure accuracy of data for analysis. Data Systems Analyst, Senior-IRIM Inst Research and Accreditation Create and maintain a data warehouse environment capable of serving the needs of both the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) Department and the campus. Serve as project leader for designated IRIM projects. Create internet-based user input and query interfaces for creating flexible, user-defined data marts from a data warehouse. Design and develop effective ways to boost data warehouse performance. Act as liaison between IRIM and IT technical staff. COB Director of Internships, Career Services & Professional Development College of Business The Director of Internships, Career Services and Professional Development leads the College of Business' career and professional development function serving business students, with direct responsibility for internship placement, professional development programming, and the cultivation of strong, lasting relationships between the College and the employer community. This role is the primary architect of the business student experience that connects classroom learning to professional practice - from securing and overseeing internships, to running signature events such as Company Days, etiquette lunch and dinners, the executive speaker series, and facilitating executive mentoring and preparing students to compete confidently for the roles they want after graduation. Health & Safety Specialist Public Safety Develop, revise, implement and monitor University health, safety and environmental programs/activities to ensure compliance with federal, state and local occupational safety, health and environmental regulations. Administrative Secretary College of Education Provide secretarial services and administrative assistance to Dean, Executive Director, or equivalent-level administrator. Athletic Academic Program Specialist Intercollegiate Athletics Assist in the administration as well as the continuous development and implementation of a comprehensive support program for all student-athletes in compliance with University, MAC and NCAA regulations. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 60bb1d59 Last Name (required) 6e856406 Email (required) d82c2349 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Report a Title