    "https://careers.emich.edu/jobs/staff-graduate-assistant-mshrod-china-ypsilanti-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Staff Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Staff Graduate Assistant - MSHROD China - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Home Working at EMU Benefits & Wellness About HR Existing Applicant Log-in Kiosk mode Staff Graduate Assistant - MSHROD China Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States College of Business Academic & Student Affairs Graduate Assistant Temporary Opening on: Aug 31 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Staff Graduate Assistant - MSHROD China Employee Classification: GS - Graduate Student - Stipend Pay Grade: GS 0 Division: Academic and Student Affairs Subdivision: MSHROD China Department: College of Business Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary The scope of work potentially includes but is not limited to assisting with translations and communications with EMU partners in China, working with faculty in the EMU Management Department on their pedagogical and research activities pertaining to the MSHROD China program, and other office support type activities. The Graduate Assistant receives a stipend and a tuition waiver. Principal Duties and Responsibilities The Graduate Assistant (GA) will be assigned to work closely with one or more faculty members, assisting with scholarly and teaching-related activities associated with the MSHROD China Program. The scope of work potentially includes, but is not limited to, assisting with translations and communications with EMU partners in China, working with faculty in the EMU Management Department on their pedagogical and research activities pertaining to the MSHROD China program, and other office support-type activities. Assist faculty/staff with research related to projects, teaching related support tasks other assignments that require the skills of graduate students. The Graduate Assistant receives a stipend and a tuition waiver. Other Departmental related duties as required. Minimum Qualifications: Admission and enrollment in a graduate program. Ability to work up to 20 hours per week. Undergraduate GPA of 3.0 required for new graduate students. For GA reappointments, maintenance of a 67% course completion. A GA must maintain a GPA of 3.0 to continue. Enrollment in at least 6 credits for Fall and Winter Semesters. Area-Specific Requirements: Must be able to read, write and speak fluently in Mandarin Chinese. Preference will be given to graduate students who are able to work two consecutive semesters. Proficiency to Microsoft Office Software- Word, Excel, PowerPoint. Strong oral and written communication skills in Mandarin and English. Able to work with statistical and survey software. Preferred Qualifications: N/A Special Instructions: N/A Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert 83ecae18 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Business College of Business Categories Academic & Student Affairs Academic & Student Affairs First Name (required) 526751d3 Last Name (required) b90a250d Email (required) cc112614 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Institutional Research Analyst, Senior (IRIM) Inst Research and Accreditation Develop and maintain systems that enhance the utility of the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) data warehouse. Develop and maintain online and automated reporting facilities and interactive dashboards. Provide statistical support and enrollment forecasting. Collect and audit primary and secondary data sources to assure accuracy of data for analysis. Data Systems Analyst, Senior-IRIM Inst Research and Accreditation Create and maintain a data warehouse environment capable of serving the needs of both the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) Department and the campus. Serve as project leader for designated IRIM projects. Create internet-based user input 