      "title": "Part Time Lecturer",
      "description": "Part Time Lecturer - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Home Working at EMU Benefits & Wellness About HR Existing Applicant Log-in Kiosk mode Part Time Lecturer Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States College of Arts and Sciences Academic & Student Affairs College of Arts & Sciences Part Time Lecturer Opening on: Aug 18 2026 Closing on: Sep 10 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Part Time Lecturer Employee Classification: LL - Adjunct Lecturer Pay Grade: LL 00 Division: Academic and Student Affairs Subdivision: School of Music and Dance Department: College of Arts and Sciences Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary The Eastern Michigan University School of Music & Dance invites applications for a Part-Time Lecturer in Dance. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses in Dance on an as-needed basis. Please note that this part-time appointment (salaried only, no benefits) requires in-person instruction on Eastern Michigan University’s campus in Ypsilanti, Michigan. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Teaching includes class instruction in Dance courses, as needed and based on the successful candidate’s expertise. Teaching may also include a number of particular obligations which employees are expected to fulfill, including but not limited to: meeting with students during and outside of assigned classes, assessing student work and performance, preparing syllabi and course materials, providing copies of syllabi and course materials to their supervisor on request, and assigning and submitting grades in accordance with established Eastern Michigan University schedules. Minimum Qualifications: MFA in Dance or equivalent Preferred Qualifications: Professional experience in at least one modern dance company; priority given to national (outside of Michigan) companies Record of exceptional teaching, master classes, and guest residencies. This artist must be a teacher first--able to reach and inspire the next generation of dance artists. Special Instructions: Interested candidates should provide a cover letter, curriculum vitae/resume, and a list of three current references. Review will commence immediately. The Fall 2026 semester at EMU begins on August 31, 2026 Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert bcb8ca25 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Arts and Sciences College of Arts and Sciences Categories Academic & Student Affairs College of Arts & Sciences Academic & Student Affairs College of Arts & Sciences First Name (required) 0d084053 Last Name (required) 4c0ba880 Email (required) b0c36dc4 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Institutional Research Analyst, Senior (IRIM) Inst Research and Accreditation Develop and maintain systems that enhance the utility of the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) data warehouse. Develop and maintain online and automated reporting facilities and interactive dashboards. Provide statistical support and enrollment forecasting. Collect and audit primary and secondary data sources to assure accuracy of data for analysis. Data Systems Analyst, Senior-IRIM Inst Research and Accreditation Create and maintain a data warehouse environment capable of serving the needs of both the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) Department and the campus. Serve as project leader for designated IRIM projects. Create internet-based user input and query interfaces for creating flexible, user-defined data marts from a data warehouse. Design and develop effective ways to boost data warehouse performance. Act as liaison between IRIM and IT technical staff. COB Director of Internships, Career Services & Professional Development College of Business The Director