      "title": "Part Time Lecturer (Nursing)",
      "description": "Part Time Lecturer (Nursing) - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Home Working at EMU Benefits & Wellness About HR Existing Applicant Log-in Kiosk mode Part Time Lecturer (Nursing) Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States College of Health and Human Serv Academic & Student Affairs College of Health & Human Services Adjunct Lecturer Opening on: Aug 21 2026 Closing on: Sep 13 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Part Time Lecturer (Nursing) Employee Classification: LL - Adjunct Lecturer Pay Grade: LL 00 Division: Academic and Student Affairs Subdivision: School of Nursing Department: College of Health and Human Serv Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary The School of Nursing is searching for part-time lecturers (PTLs) with experience in community health to work with our full-time faculty on an as-needed basis to teach clinical nursing courses. Principal Duties and Responsibilities The primary professional responsibility of the Employee is teaching. Employees are expected to develop and maintain their professional skills in order to ensure high quality education for their students. Teaching may include a number of particular obligations which employees are expected to fulfill, including but not limited to: meeting with students during and outside of assigned classes, assessing student work and performance, preparing syllabi and course materials, providing copies of syllabi and course materials to their supervisor on request, and assigning and submitting grades in accordance with established Eastern Michigan University schedules. Perform related departmental duties as required. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor of Science in Nursing required. Active, unencumbered license as a professional nurse (RN) in the state of Michigan. Two years of recent and applicable clinical experience required. Preferred Qualifications: MSN preferred. Prior experience with teaching clinical and/or undergraduate students is ideal but not required. Special Instructions: Applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and copy of nursing license. Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert c64b34a5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Health and Human Serv College of Health and Human Serv Categories Academic & Student Affairs College of Health & Human Services Academic & Student Affairs College of Health & Human Services First Name (required) 6c7438d0 Last Name (required) fefb3c9a Email (required) a75e53eb Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Institutional Research Analyst, Senior (IRIM) Inst Research and Accreditation Develop and maintain systems that enhance the utility of the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) data warehouse. Develop and maintain online and automated reporting facilities and interactive dashboards. Provide statistical support and enrollment forecasting. Collect and audit primary and secondary data sources to assure accuracy of data for analysis. Data Systems Analyst, Senior-IRIM Inst Research and Accreditation Create and maintain a data warehouse environment capable of serving the needs of both the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) Department and the campus. Serve as project leader for designated IRIM projects. Create internet-based user input and query interfaces for creating flexible, user-defined data marts from a data warehouse. Design and develop effective ways to boost data warehouse performance. Act as liaison between IRIM and IT technical staff. COB Director of Internships, Career Services & Professional Development College of Business The Director of Internships, Career Services and Professional Development leads the College of Business' career and professional development fu