      "title": "Full-Time Lecturer (Social Work)",
      "description": "Full-Time Lecturer (Social Work) - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Home Working at EMU Benefits & Wellness About HR Existing Applicant Log-in Kiosk mode Full-Time Lecturer (Social Work) Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States College of Health and Human Serv Academic & Student Affairs College of Health & Human Services Full Time Lecturer Opening on: Aug 7 2026 Closing on: Sep 11 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Full-Time Lecturer (Social Work) Employee Classification: LE - Lecturer 16 and 24 Pay Pay Grade: LE 01 Division: Academic and Student Affairs Subdivision: School of Social Work Department: College of Health and Human Serv Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary Teach specific courses within the School of Social Work. Background in Social Work and familiarity with the curriculum and teaching are essential. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Teach contractual load of courses as assigned by the department or school. Assign and submit grades in accordance with established University schedules. Keep posted office hours during the week which are scheduled at times most beneficial to students. Provide enrollment data and such other information as corrected class lists, etc. as may be required by the University. Engage in pursuits that enable them to remain current in their respective disciplines. Confer periodically with the Department Head/School Director on curriculum and instruction issues. Provide other support service to the department, college and/or university, if applicable. Perform related departmental duties as required. Minimum Qualifications: Lecturer I: Master's degree, or a Bachelor's degree plus thirty (30) graduate credit hours in a discipline directly related to the teaching assignment, or equivalent, as determined by the Department Head/School Director. Lecturer II: Master's degree plus thirty (30) hours toward a terminal degree, All But Dissertation status (ABD) or equivalent, as determined by the Department Head/School Director. Lecturer III: An earned doctorate, terminal degree that is recognized as equivalent to the doctorate in the applicable Departmental Evaluation Document, or equivalent as determined by the Department Head/School Director. Preferred Qualifications: Preferred LLMSW or LMSW. Special Instructions: Applicants must submit the following materials: • A cover letter describing interest in the position and relevant qualifications and experience. • A curriculum vitae, including names and contact information for two professional references. Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert 3e9d4bf7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Health and Human Serv College of Health and Human Serv Categories Academic & Student Affairs College of Health & Human Services Academic & Student Affairs College of Health & Human Services First Name (required) f9b5e076 Last Name (required) e76ab305 Email (required) c25a38c0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Institutional Research Analyst, Senior (IRIM) Inst Research and Accreditation Develop and maintain systems that enhance the utility of the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) data warehouse. Develop and maintain online and automated reporting facilities and interactive dashboards. Provide statistical support and enrollment forecasting. Collect and audit primary and secondary data sources to assure accuracy of data for analysis. Data Systems Analyst, Senior-IRIM Inst Research and Accreditation Create and maintain a data warehouse environment capable of serving the needs of both the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) Department and the campus. Serve as project leader for designated IRIM projects. Create in