    "https://careers.emich.edu/jobs/custodian-ypsilanti-michigan-united-states-ca37ef22-3c08-47ed-8a1a-c03f483caf46": {
      "title": "Custodian",
      "description": "Custodian - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Home Working at EMU Benefits & Wellness About HR Existing Applicant Log-in Kiosk mode Custodian Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Facilities Business & Finance Staff Full Time Opening on: Sep 11 2026 Closing on: Sep 18 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Custodian Employee Classification: FM Pay Grade: FM 06* Division: Business and Finance Subdivision: Custodial Services Department: Facilities Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary Perform routine and heavy cleaning, and upkeep of University buildings and facilities. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Clean and maintain floor surfaces and stairways by sweeping, mop-ping, stripping, sealing, refinishing, and polishing, using hand and/or mechanical cleaning, scrubbing and buffing equipment. Clean mirrors, blackboards, interior glass and windows, drinking fountains, ceilings, walls, doors and other appliances and equipment. Vacuum and clean carpeted floors, stairways and upholstered furniture. Clean carpeted floors as needed. Clean lavatories and fixtures. Empty waste containers, ash trays and cigarette urns; and pick up refuse in buildings. Empty waste containers outside building entrances. Stock lavatories and other applicable rooms with necessary supplies such as soap, toilet paper and towels, and maintain an inventory of various supplies and equipment in accordance with specific instructions. Replace burned-out light bulbs. Clean, dust and polish items such as cases, ledges, furniture, equipment, fixtures, furnishings, venetian blinds and window casings. Remove snow and ice from building entrances, as directed. Move and arrange furniture, supplies, equipment and furnishings, as required, to perform assigned cleaning or to set up for various meetings and events. Maintain cleanliness of work and storage areas and all supplies and equipment used in the performance of duties. Report any damage, malfunction, irregularities and/or potential hazards in equipment or supplies to supervisor. Lock and unlock rooms and buildings. Perform related Departmental duties, as required. Minimum Qualifications: Ability to read, write, interpret instructions and perform basic arithmetic, typically acquired through the completion of a high school education, is necessary. Ability to perform physically active work of a medium-heavy nature, requiring frequent walking, climbing, pushing, pulling, stooping, kneeling and crouching activity to perform routine cleaning functions; and frequent lifting requiring the exertion of up to 50 pounds of force to lift a mop bucket, vacuum, ladder, or other supplies and equipment, is necessary. Ability to meet Departmental standards of reasonable personal hygiene is necessary. Preferred Qualifications: Knowledge of cleaning techniques and operation of custodial equipment is desirable. Additional Information: Salary: FM 06* = $17.39 an hour/$36,171 annually Shift: Monday - Friday 5:00 AM to 1:30 PM Location: Sherzer/Hoover Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert 8f4f209f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Facilities Facilities Categories Business & Finance Business & Finance First Name (required) 5121e808 Last Name (required) ca1d22a4 Email (required) 75278bb3 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Custodian Facilities Salary: FM 06* = $17.39 an hour/$36,171 annually\nShift: Monday - Friday 5:00 AM to 1:30 PM\nLocation: Sherzer/Hoover Site Coordinator Engage@EMU The Site Coordinator is a full-time position with responsibilities that include planning and executing the facilitation of a daily after-school program, planning activities for youth, managing and coaching a small staff, and recruiting and enrolling students. Coordinator, Audio Visual Services Student Life University Event Services is seeking an experienced Audio/Visual Event Services Specialist to lead the audio/visual operations that support major events. This hands-on role is responsible for operating, maintaining, troubleshooting, designing, and improving AV systems while providing on-site technical support for large-scale events, conferences, performances, and campus programs. Institutional Research Analyst, Senior (IRIM) Inst Research and Accreditation Develop and maintain systems that enhance the utility of the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) data warehouse. Develop and maintain online and automated reporting facilities and interactive dashboards. Provide statistical support and enrollment forecasting. Collect and audit primary and secondary data sources to assure accuracy of data for analysis. Data Systems Analyst, Senior-IRIM Inst Research and Accreditation Create and maintain a data warehouse environment capable of serving the needs of both the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) Department and the campus. Serve as project leader for designated IRIM projects. Create internet-based user input and query interfaces for creating flexible, user-defined data marts from a data warehouse. Design and develop effective ways to boost data warehouse performance. Act as liaison between IRIM and IT technical staff. COB Director of Internships, Career Services & Professional Development College of Business The Director of Internships, Career Services and Professional Development leads the College of Business' career and professional development function serving business students, with direct responsibility for internship placement, professional development programming, and the cultivation of strong, lasting relationships between the College and the employer community. This role is the primary architect of the business student experience that connects classroom learning to professional practice - from securing and overseeing internships, to running signature events such as Company Days, etiquette lunch and dinners, the executive speaker series, and facilitating executive mentoring and preparing students to compete confidently for the roles they want after graduation. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 899cb43a Last Name (required) 2570e6ba Email (required) c43b8a43 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Report a Title IX Incident Accessibility Privacy Statement Annual Security Report Copyright © 2022 All Rights Reserved by Eastern Michigan University . Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"
