    "https://careers.emich.edu/jobs/site-coordinator-ypsilanti-michigan-united-states-d2367609-89aa-4077-b617-4f183149ec0c": {
      "title": "Site Coordinator",
      "description": "Site Coordinator - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Home Working at EMU Benefits & Wellness About HR Existing Applicant Log-in Kiosk mode Site Coordinator Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Engage@EMU Academic & Student Affairs Staff Full Time Opening on: Sep 10 2026 Closing on: Sep 24 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Site Coordinator Employee Classification: PT Pay Grade: PT 07 Division: Academic and Student Affairs Subdivision: Stdy Chldrn and Family Department: Engage@EMU Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary Responsible for implementing school age educational activities at an assigned location. Coordinate activities that include academic learning experiences, field trips and site-based liaison among program staff, school staff, community partners, students and parents., Principal Duties and Responsibilities Maintain efficient learning environment for a quality educationally-focused after school program. Set-up, open and close daily after school program site; prepare daily snacks. Coordinate activities with program teaching staff and act as liaison to regular school staff. Document and maintain daily attendance, homework activity and other personnel and student records, as necessary, to meet state and federal database management requirements and deadlines. Coordinate activity flow, time and facility management. Assist with teaching activities; develop activities that integrate with academic core time. Participant in curriculum development and integration. Assist with the application of technology to science and literacy curriculum components. Interact effectively with students, parents, staff, community partners and University personnel on a daily basis. Supervise student assistances; mentor and evaluate pre-student teachers. Maintain a safe and orderly learning environment. Perform related departmental duties as required. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelors degree in an educational or youth related field is required, at least 12 hours in child development, child psychology, early childhood education or related course work is required. Must demonstrate a mature attitude in dealing with students, parents, school district staff and community partners. Evidence of organization, supervisory and interpersonal skills for establishing good relationships with staff, teachers, parents and students. Must be willing to participate in additional training and workshops as designated by the after school program. Must be CPR/First Aid certified or willing to obtain certification. Preferred Qualifications: Teaching certificate is preferred. Work experience at a K-12 school, especially in an informal or after school setting is preferred. Special Instructions: N/A Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert b95e2adb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Engage@EMU Engage@EMU Categories Academic & Student Affairs Academic & Student Affairs First Name (required) 5d7e1b1a Last Name (required) 3e6ae5bf Email (required) 9855d9ca Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Custodian Facilities Salary: FM 06* = $17.39 an hour/$36,171 annually\nShift: Monday - Friday 5:00 AM to 1:30 PM\nLocation: Sherzer/Hoover Site Coordinator Engage@EMU The Site Coordinator is a full-time position with responsibilities that include planning and executing the facilitation of a daily after-school program, planning activities for youth, managing and coaching a small staff, and recruiting and enrolling students. Coordinator, Audio Visual Services Student Life University Event Services is seeking an experienced Audio/Visual Event Services Specialist to lead the audio/visual operations that support major events. This hands-on role is responsible for operating, maintaining, troubleshooting, designing, and improving AV systems while providing on-site technical support for large-scale events, conferences, performances, and campus programs. Institutional Research Analyst, Senior (IRIM) Inst Research and Accreditation Develop and maintain systems that enhance the utility of the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) data warehouse. Develop and maintain online and automated reporting facilities and interactive dashboards. Provide statistical support and enrollment forecasting. Collect and audit primary and secondary data sources to assure accuracy of data for analysis. Data Systems Analyst, Senior-IRIM Inst Research and Accreditation Create and maintain a data warehouse environment capable of serving the needs of both the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) Department and the campus. Serve as project leader for designated IRIM projects. Create internet-based user input and query interfaces for creating flexible, user-defined data marts from a data warehouse. Design and develop effective ways to boost data warehouse performance. Act as liaison between IRIM and IT technical staff. COB Director of Internships, Career Services & Professional Development College of Business The Director of Internships, Career Services and Professional Development leads the College of Business' career and professional development function serving business students, with direct responsibility for internship placement, professional development programming, and the cultivation of strong, lasting relationships between the College and the employer community. This role is the primary architect of the business student experience that connects classroom learning to professional practice - from securing and overseeing internships, to running signature events such as Company Days, etiquette lunch and dinners, the executive speaker series, and facilitating executive mentoring and preparing students to compete confidently for the roles they want after graduation. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 6d51f200 Last Name (required) 3f2ad313 Email (required) f7b212e8 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Report a Title IX Incident Accessibility Privacy Statement Annual Security Report Copyright © 2022 All Rights Reserved by Eastern Michigan University . Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"
