    "https://careers.emich.edu/jobs/director-career-development-ypsilanti-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Director, Career Development",
      "description": "Director, Career Development - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Home Working at EMU Benefits & Wellness About HR Existing Applicant Log-in Kiosk mode Director, Career Development Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Academic Programming and Services Academic & Student Affairs Staff Full Time Opening on: Sep 16 2026 Closing on: Oct 16 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Director, Career Development Employee Classification: AP - Administrative Professional Pay Grade: AP 09 Division: Academic and Student Affairs Subdivision: Univ Advising and Career Devel Ctr Department: Academic Programming and Services Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary Provide strategic and administrative leadership of the team for career development programs, initiatives, partnerships, technology, communications, and outreach within the University Career Development Center. Work closely with University partners to develop and implement innovative approaches to career exploration, career readiness, professional development, experiential learning, employer engagement, and student success. Expand the reach and impact of career development across the University and ensure students have access to high-quality career resources, experiences, relationships, and opportunities. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Provide leadership for the development, implementation, assessment, and continuous improvement of career development programs and initiatives serving EMU students and alumni. Help develop and execute a comprehensive vision for career development that integrates career exploration and preparation throughout the student experience. Identify opportunities to innovate and expand programming in response to changing student needs, employer expectations, emerging technologies, economic conditions, and workforce trends. Build strong partnerships with academic colleges, departments, faculty, advisors, student-success professionals, alumni engagement, advancement, and other University units. Develop innovative strategies for engaging students earlier and more consistently in career exploration, professional development, experiential learning, networking, and career preparation. Partner with employers, alumni, community organizations, and industry leaders to create meaningful connections and opportunities for students. Expand opportunities for internships, experiential learning, mentoring, employer engagement, networking, and other experiences that prepare students for successful transitions from college to career. Develop and coordinate programs, workshops, events, resources, and other experiences that strengthen career readiness and professional competencies. Provide leadership and support for career fairs, employer engagement programs, networking opportunities, industry-focused events, alumni career programs, and other signature experiences. Develop strategies to ensure career development programs and resources are accessible and responsive to EMU's broad and diverse student population. Serve as a resource and representative of the Center and provide leadership on career development, partnerships, marketing, and outreach. Assist in developing and implementing marketing, communications, and outreach strategies that increase awareness and engagement. Collaborate on continuous improvement of the Center's website, digital resources, social media, communications, and other platforms. Explore and advance emerging technologies, including artificial intelligence and digital career platforms, to expand access, personalize the student experience, and prepare students for a changing workplace. Use data, assessment, student and employer feedback, and workforce trends to evaluate programs, demonstrate impact, and guide strategic decision-making. Develop meaningful measures of student engagement and career outcomes and contribute to a culture of assessment and continuous improvement. Assist with annual and periodic reports, career outcomes information, employment trend analyses, and other materials demonstrating impact. Assist with development and monitoring of the Center budget and strategic deployment of resources. Supervise, coach, and develop assigned professional, support, and student staff. Represent the Department at professional conferences, meetings, employer and community events, and on University committees. Maintain knowledge of national trends and emerging practices in career development, higher education, workforce development, experiential learning, and student success. Identify opportunities for partnerships, sponsorships, external resources, and collaborations that expand career development opportunities for EMU students. Adhere to applicable Eastern Michigan University policies, rules, regulations, and operational procedures. Perform related departmental duties, as required. Minimum Qualifications: Knowledge of higher education, career development, workforce and recruiting trends, experiential learning, communications and marketing strategies, employer engagement, and program development typically acquired through completion of a master's degree in Higher Education, College Student Personnel, Counseling, Human Resources, Business, Communications, Marketing, or a related field is required. At least five years of progressively responsible professional experience in career development, higher education, workforce development, employer relations, student success, experiential learning, or a closely related area is required. Demonstrated experience supervising, developing, or leading staff is required. Demonstrated ability to develop and implement programs, initiatives, or partnerships from concept through execution is required. Strong interpersonal, written, verbal, organizational, and collaborative leadership skills are required. Demonstrated ability to establish productive relationships with students, faculty, staff, administrators, employers, alumni, and external partners is required. Experience using technology, data, assessment, and feedback to improve programs, services, or constituent experiences is required. Preferred Qualifications: Direct experience in career services, career development, employer relations, experiential learning, workforce development, academic advising, or another student-success function in higher education is preferred. Experience developing innovative career programs, employer partnerships, experiential learning opportunities, or student engagement initiatives is preferred. Experience with career management platforms, CRM systems, digital engagement tools, artificial intelligence, or other emerging technologies relevant to career development is preferred. Special Instructions: N/A Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert 806d3daa Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Academic Programming and Services Academic Programming and Services Categories Academic & Student Affairs Academic & Student Affairs First Name (required) 473bbf3f Last Name (required) 5e57c77a Email (required) 5ec1f3dc Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Director, Career Development Academic Programming and Services Provide strategic and administrative leadership of the team for career development programs, initiatives, partnerships, technology, communications, and outreach within the University Career Development Center. Work closely with University partners to develop and implement innovative approaches to career exploration, career readiness, professional development, experiential learning, employer engagement, and student success. Expand the reach and impact of career development across the University and ensure students have access to high-quality career resources, experiences, relationships, and opportunities. Case Manager, Dean of Students Student Life The Case Manager coordinates campus support systems and resources to implement a plan of care for students in need, and oversees the case management program for sensitive student problems. Serving as a member of the Student Intervention Team (SIT), the Case Manager assists the SIT Chair with overall case management by triage referrals, coordinating interventions, tracking students' completion of recommendations. This person works closely with other campus resource providers, clinicians, student affairs and academic units, and community support systems in coordinating a response that balances the needs of individual students with the safety and welfare of the University community. Custodian Facilities Salary: FM 06* = $17.39 an hour/$36,171 annually\nShift: Tuesday - Saturday 11:00 AM to 7:30 PM\nLocation: Float, Main Campus Customer Service Representative II Public Safety Under limited supervision, perform various duties in support of office customer service functions and related operational activities, either in person or over the telephone, or in correspondence which require a working knowledge of a wider variety and complex program policies, procedures and regulations. Custodian Facilities Salary: FM 06* = $17.39 an hour/$36,171 annually\nShift: Sunday - Thursday 1:30 PM to 10:00 PM\nLocation: Judy Sturgis Hill Custodian Facilities Salary: FM 06* = $17.39 an hour/$36,171 annually\nShift: Sunday - Thursday 5:00 AM to 1:30 PM\nLocation: Float, Main Campus Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 3a869e1b Last Name (required) 67e51e9c Email (required) eef6bbdf Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Report a Title IX Incident Accessibility Privacy Statement Annual Security Report Copyright © 2022 All Rights Reserved by Eastern Michigan University . Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise