    "https://careers.emich.edu/jobs/benefits-coordinator-ypsilanti-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Benefits Coordinator",
      "description": "Benefits Coordinator - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Home Working at EMU Benefits & Wellness About HR Existing Applicant Log-in Kiosk mode Benefits Coordinator Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States University Human Resources Human resources Staff Full Time Opening on: Sep 24 2026 Closing on: Oct 9 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Benefits Coordinator Employee Classification: AH - Administrative Non-Exempt Pay Grade: AH 02 Division: Academic and Student Affairs Subdivision: Total Rewards Department: University Human Resources Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary Under general direction, support the efficient and effective operation of the Benefits function by counseling employees in all health and welfare programs, leave of absence (LOA), and workers’ compensation. Oversees health and welfare programs, leave of absence (LOA), workers’ compensation, and system data entry and administration across different platforms and vendor reporting systems. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Counsels employees regarding all health and welfare programs, LOA, and workers’ compensation. Assists in the handling of routine benefits, LOA and worker compensation inquiries, and complaints and issues to ensure quick, equitable, and courteous resolution. Leads the administration, tracking, and system reporting for LOA and workers’ compensation programs to ensure they are administered according to plan provisions and company regulatory guidelines. Assists in the administration of benefit plans, employee elections, and deductions. Performs basic data entry into systems and databases primarily for benefit plan enrollment, deductions, benefit changes, LOA, and workers’ compensation. Assists with other changes including but not limited to new hires, promotions, transfers, salary changes, retirements, and terminations. Assists with university-wide initiatives, such as benefits orientation, annual open enrollment, retirement programs, and wellness programs. Collaborates with Payroll to understand and set due dates for personnel and benefit-related actions; monitors payroll cycles and paces work to meet established deadlines. Audits benefit vendor/carrier invoices and works directly with benefit vendors to reconcile discrepancies, and to create and submit payment requests for approval. Modifies query variables to run standard reports. As directed, generates more complex and ad hoc reports; completes Request for Services (RFS) forms and works with IT to create new reports as needed. Liaises with HR, Business and Finance, and academic departments to provide technical assistance, troubleshoot, investigate, and resolve problems, determine due dates for personnel and benefits-related actions, and provide training support. Documents and maintains procedural manuals and policies for HRIS and benefit vendor databases. Analyzes data flows to identify process improvements and recommends and helps implement workflows to streamline HR operations and benefits administration. As directed, participates in efforts to research, recommend, and implement new HR modules or systems for benefits, LOA, and workers’ compensation administration. Cross-trains designated staff to provide assistance during peak periods of activity. Stays abreast of trends, laws, regulations, best practices, and technologies related to assigned functional areas. Assists with planning and implementing special events and works on special projects. Perform related departmental duties as required. Minimum Qualifications: A bachelor's degree, preferably in Business Administration, Computer Information Systems, Human Resource Management, or a related behavioral science field, OR eight years of equivalent work experience; OR an equivalent combination of education and experience that demonstrates the ability to perform all essential duties of the position is required. Working knowledge of Human Resources principles and practices, typically acquired through at least one year of work experience in a Human Resources related position, OR through a combination of graduate-level coursework and related internship experience is required. Demonstrated independent judgment, strong verbal and written communication skills, and the ability to maintain confidentiality, meet deadlines, and interact with all levels within an organization are required. Preferred Qualifications: Personal computing skills, including working knowledge of word processing, spreadsheet, and database management software (specifically Microsoft Word, Excel, and Access) are required. Proficiency with Banner ERP and Crystal or Argos report-writing tools is preferred. Knowledge of the Affordable Care Act (ACA), Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA), and EEO laws and regulations is preferred. Experience working in a higher education or healthcare setting, a unionized environment, or another fast-paced, dynamic HR environment is preferred. Special Instructions: Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Similar Jobs Institutional Research Analyst, Senior (IRIM) Inst Research and Accreditation Develop and maintain systems that enhance the utility of the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) data warehouse. Develop and maintain online and automated reporting facilities and interactive dashboards. Provide statistical support and enrollment forecasting. Collect and audit primary and secondary data sources to assure accuracy of data for analysis. Data Systems Analyst, Senior-IRIM Inst Research and Accreditation Create and maintain a data warehouse environment capable of serving the needs of both the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) Department and the campus. Serve as project leader for designated IRIM projects. Create internet-based user input and query interfaces for creating flexible, user-defined data marts from a data warehouse. Design and develop effective ways to boost data warehouse performance. Act as liaison between IRIM and IT technical staff. Benefits Coordinator University Human Resources Eastern Michigan University is seeking a Benefits Coordinator to support the smooth, efficient operation of our Benefits function. In this role, you’ll counsel employees on health and welfare programs, leaves of absence, and workers’ compensation, while overseeing related system administration and reporting. You’ll collaborate across HR, Payroll, and campus departments, assist with major initiatives like Open Enrollment and Benefits Orientation, audit vendor invoices, and help improve workflows and processes. If you’re detail‑oriented, customer‑focused, and ready to make an impact in a dynamic HR environment, we’d love to have you join our team. Medical Dir for School of Physician Asst Studies College of Health and Human Serv The Medical Director supports the Program Director in ensuring that both didactic instruction and supervised clinical practice experiences meet current practice standards as they relate to the Physician Assistant role in providing patient care. Dir, Staff & Command Programs Placeholder1 The Director, Staff and Command Programs directs specific programs for Staff and Command across multiple locations within in the College of Arts and Sciences. The director manages all administrative and operational activities in support of this operation, ensures student success, manages public safety community partnerships, and explores its possible national and global expansion. Coordinator, Student Business Processes Business and Finance Plan and supervise administrative, operational, and technical activities with moderate authority to make commitments on behalf of Student Business Services. This may include tracking and monitoring student refunds, billing, student concerns, and processing in various vendor/partner computer applications. Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Report a Title IX Incident Accessibility Privacy Statement Annual Security Report Copyright © 2022 All Rights Reserved by Eastern