    "https://careers.emich.edu/jobs/manager-university-support-services-ypsilanti-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Manager, University Support Services",
      "description": "Manager, University Support Services - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Home Working at EMU Benefits & Wellness About HR Existing Applicant Log-in Kiosk mode Manager, University Support Services Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Business and Finance Business & Finance Staff Full Time Opening on: Sep 18 2026 Closing on: Oct 2 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Manager, University Support Services Employee Classification: PT Pay Grade: PT 07 Division: Business and Finance Subdivision: Purchasing Department: Business and Finance Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary Administer and supervise EMU's Logistics Services that include: Shipping/Receiving and Mail Services, Move Requests, and Inventory Operations. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Administer and supervise University's Logistic Services. Administer and manage central receiving activities within Purchasing Department software system(s). Develop best-in-class processes for Mail Services, Inventory, and Shipping/Receiving activities. Responsible for daily and monthly reporting for mail service, central receiving, and surplus inventory levels. Maintain and support central store vehicles in collaboration with Fleet Management. Schedule and oversee move requests from university departments, in collaboration with the Physical Plant as necessary. Respond to inquiries from University staff regarding policies and procedures of all areas of responsibility. Provide excellent customer service to the University community for all areas of responsibility. Interview, train, and evaluate directly supervised staff, including student staff. Other activities as assigned by Director, Purchasing and Procurement. Minimum Qualifications: The completion of a Bachelor's degree in Business or equivalent experience is required in order to manage and perform these supervisory and operational duties. Three years (3) of directly-related logistics experience providing a working knowledge of shipping, receiving, mail services, surplus property inventory, other warehousing functions, and ERP systems, including at least two (2) years of supervisory experience, are required. Preferred Qualifications: N/A Special Instructions: N/A Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert 03092c41 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Business and Finance Business and Finance Categories Business & Finance Business & Finance First Name (required) 4717cb6b Last Name (required) c4ccc438 Email (required) 903ec342 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Institutional Research Analyst, Senior (IRIM) Inst Research and Accreditation Develop and maintain systems that enhance the utility of the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) data warehouse. Develop and maintain online and automated reporting facilities and interactive dashboards. Provide statistical support and enrollment forecasting. Collect and audit primary and secondary data sources to assure accuracy of data for analysis. Data Systems Analyst, Senior-IRIM Inst Research and Accreditation Create and maintain a data warehouse environment capable of serving the needs of both the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) Department and the campus. Serve as project leader for designated IRIM projects. Create internet-based user input and query interfaces for creating flexible, user-defined data marts from a data warehouse. Design and develop effective ways to boost data warehouse performance. Act as liaison between IRIM and IT technical staff. Benefits Coordinator University Human Resources Eastern Michigan University is seeking a Benefits Coordinator to support the smooth, efficient operation of our Benefits function. In this role, you’ll counsel employees on health and welfare programs, leaves of absence, and workers’ compensation, while overseeing related system administration and reporting. You’ll collaborate across HR, Payroll, and campus departments, assist with major initiatives like Open Enrollment and Benefits Orientation, audit vendor invoices, and help improve workflows and processes. If you’re detail‑oriented, customer‑focused, and ready to make an impact in a dynamic HR environment, we’d love to have you join our team. Medical Dir for School of Physician Asst Studies College of Health and Human Serv The Medical Director supports the Program Director in ensuring that both didactic instruction and supervised clinical practice experiences meet current practice standards as they relate to the Physician Assistant role in providing patient care. Dir, Staff & Command Programs Placeholder1 The Director, Staff and Command Programs directs specific programs for Staff and Command across multiple locations within in the College of Arts and Sciences. The director manages all administrative and operational activities in support of this operation, ensures student success, manages public safety community partnerships, and explores its possible national and global expansion. Coordinator, Student Business Processes Business and Finance Plan and supervise administrative, operational, and technical activities with moderate authority to make commitments on behalf of Student Business Services. This may include tracking and monitoring student refunds, billing, student concerns, and processing in various vendor/partner computer applications. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 2c075a2a Last Name (required) 8e6b8e23 Email (required) 0600637f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Report a Title IX Incident Accessibility Privacy Statement Annual Security Report Copyright © 2022 All Rights Reserved by Eastern Michigan University . Candidate