      "title": "Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Academic Advisor - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Home Working at EMU Benefits & Wellness About HR Existing Applicant Log-in Kiosk mode Academic Advisor Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Academic Programming and Services Academic & Student Affairs Staff Full Time Opening on: Sep 17 2026 Closing on: Oct 1 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Academic Advisor Employee Classification: PT Pay Grade: PT 07 Division: Academic and Student Affairs Subdivision: Director University Advising Department: Academic Programming and Services Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary Advise and counsel all assigned students on curriculum requirements, vocational information, scholarship and /or academic achievement problems. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Advise students on courses, class loads, course changes, withdrawals, transfers of credits, eligibility for credit by examination and time extensions. Provide general advisory and vocational information to students and assist in the distribution of information. Assist in administering advising programs designed for specific students, such as students with special needs, evening students, probationary students, foreign students, etc. Assist with in-service training seminars for advisors, faculty interns, graduate assistants and student advising assistants. Assist Departmental advisors concerning academic policies and procedures. Attend staff meetings and participate on University committees. If applicable to area of assignment, adhere to any and all NCAA, Mid-American Conference and Eastern Michigan University policies, rules, regulations, and operational procedures. Adhere to any and all NCAA, Mid-American Conference and Eastern Michigan University policies, rules, regulations, and operational procedures. Perform related Departmental duties as required. Minimum Qualifications: Knowledge of academic advising and counseling, course work and related degree programs, typically acquired through the completion of a bachelor’s degree is required; a master’s degree is preferred. One year of experience in a counseling-related environment, is necessary. Written and interpersonal communication skills, in order to effectively interact with students, are necessary. Personal computer knowledge is necessary. Ability to perform physically active work of a light nature including occasional lifting requiring the exertion of up to 20 pounds of force to transport materials and equipment may be necessary depending on area of assignment. Previous experience providing knowledge of academic areas of assignment may be required. Preferred Qualifications: Professional counseling licensure is desirable. Teaching experience is desirable. Special Instructions: N/A Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert 2beaae5d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Academic Programming and Services Academic Programming and Services Categories Academic & Student Affairs Academic & Student Affairs First Name (required) 91584238 Last Name (required) 61e2743c Email (required) 28174b28 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Institutional Research Analyst, Senior (IRIM) Inst Research and Accreditation Develop and maintain systems that enhance the utility of the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) data warehouse. Develop and maintain online and automated reporting facilities and interactive dashboards. Provide statistical support and enrollment forecasting. Collect and audit primary and secondary data sources to assure accuracy of data for analysis. Data Systems Analyst, Senior-IRIM Inst Research and Accreditation Create and maintain a data warehouse environment capable of serving the needs of both the Instituti